  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-1 Starting Cutscene
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Narrator
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Jose Protasio Rizal Mercado y Alonso Realonda was born on June 19,
      1861. He was a mixed blood Filipino with practically all ethnic elements. When
      Rizal was born, a pretentious new family home was made in the center of Calamba
      which Francisco Mercado inherited from his father. The house was destroyed
      before its usefulness ceased. It was destroyed during World War II, but was
      first confiscated by the Spanish Authorities in 1891.
    isLeftSide: 0
  - speakerName: Narrator
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 30089ce6c05fb8443ac124cbe58ffc7f, type: 2}
    Dialogue: "Rizal was christened when he was three days old. His godfather was
      Father Pedro Casa\xF1as. The priest who christened him was a Filipino named
      Father Rufino Collantes. Rizal\u2019s earliest training recalls the education
      of William and Alexander von Humboldt, these two 19th Century Germans whose
      achievements for the prosperity of their fatherland and the advancement of
      humanity caused them to be spoken of as the most reliable pair of brothers
      that ever lived."
    isLeftSide: 0
  - speakerName: Narrator
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 30089ce6c05fb8443ac124cbe58ffc7f, type: 2}
    Dialogue: At 3 he learned his letters, having insisted upon being taught to read
      and being allowed to share the lessons of an older sister. He spent a lot of
      his time in the church, carefully observing people as his pastime.
    isLeftSide: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 30089ce6c05fb8443ac124cbe58ffc7f, type: 2}
    Dialogue: 'Ate!! Can I please learn what you''re learning? Pretty please? '
    isLeftSide: 1
  - speakerName: Saturnina Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 30089ce6c05fb8443ac124cbe58ffc7f, type: 2}
    Dialogue: 'Okay, Jose. You can try and learn what I''m learning. '
    isLeftSide: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 30089ce6c05fb8443ac124cbe58ffc7f, type: 2}
    Dialogue: Thank you Ate!!
    isLeftSide: 1
  - speakerName: Narrator
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 30089ce6c05fb8443ac124cbe58ffc7f, type: 2}
    Dialogue: He spent a lot of his time in the church, carefully observing people
      as his pastime.
    isLeftSide: 1
  - speakerName: Spanish Priest
    speakerType: 1
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 30089ce6c05fb8443ac124cbe58ffc7f, type: 2}
    Dialogue: You should go home and study, young man.
    isLeftSide: 0
